ok - fm-status: a plain line carries the clock's stamp and parses as the supervisor reads it
ok - fm-status: --key writes a decision key that opens and closes through the classifier
ok - fm-status: --until +N[smh] becomes the recheck time rounded up to the minute
ok - fm-status: an explicit --until is kept, and a malformed or misplaced one is refused unwritten
ok - fm-status: --line appends a printed line, stamping it only when it carries no time
ok - fm-status: every usage error exits 2 and writes nothing
ok - fm-status: a failed append exits 1
ok - fm-status: the fleet ledger records a line only while the flag exists, read from config/ or --config
